    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 the full suite (33 tests) is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `bulkSignupWarning` response field for owner creation, following the codebase's existing pattern for per-owner derived snapshots (like `namesakeCount` and `customerCode`).\n\nThe rule: when **more than 80** owners have already been registered for a given day, a newly created owner is flagged `bulkSignupWarning: true`; otherwise `false`. The value is captured at creation time and returned by both the create response and subsequent `GET /api/owners/{id}` reads.\n\nChanges:\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean to the `Owner` schema (regenerates into `OwnerDto`, auto-mapped by MapStruct since the name matches).\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `bulkSignupWarning` field (`bulk_signup_warning` column) with getter/setter.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added the `BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 80` constant and an `isBulkSignup(registrationDate)` helper that counts existing owners sharing that (business-day-adjusted) registration date and returns `count > 80`. It's evaluated on create \u2014 before the new owner is saved, so the count reflects owners that already existed \u2014 mirroring the daily-limit accumulation path.\n- **Schema SQL** (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql) \u2014 added the `bulk_signup_warning` column.\n- **Data SQL** (hsqldb, mysql) \u2014 added the trailing value to the positional seed-owner INSERTs so they still match the widened table.\n\nThe Cp22 test (`bulkSignupWarning` false for a lone create) passes, along with all 33 tests in the suite.",
